      "source": [
        "# Movie Review Sentiment Analysis (NLP)\n",
        "\n",
        "## Aim\n",
        "Build a system that classifies movie reviews as **Positive** or **Negative** using NLP and machine learning.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "1. Load and explore a sentiment dataset\n",
        "2. Preprocess text and extract TF-IDF features\n",
        "3. Train multiple models and compare performance\n",
        "4. Select the best model and deploy it using a GUI\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook is designed to produce the required outputs for your PDF screenshots: preprocessing output, model comparison table, accuracy plot, confusion matrix, best model selection, and GUI prediction results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pip -q install gradio seaborn joblib scikit-learn pandas numpy matplotlib tqdm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os, sys\n",
        "\n",
        "# Make imports work whether Colab working directory is /content or the project folder.\n",
        "candidates = [\n",
        "    os.getcwd(),\n",
        "    os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'movie_review_sentiment'),\n",
        "    '/content/movie_review_sentiment',\n+        "]\n",
        "base_dir = None\n",
        "for d in candidates:\n",
        "    if os.path.exists(os.path.join(d, 'train_and_evaluate.py')):\n",
        "        base_dir = d\n",
        "        break\n",
        "if base_dir is None:\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError('train_and_evaluate.py not found. Upload the whole folder and open this notebook from inside it.')\n",
        "\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, base_dir)\n",
        "\n",
        "import train_and_evaluate as te\n",
        "\n",
        "# Run training + reporting.\n",
        "# limit_per_class controls speed. 2500 is a good balance for Colab.\n",
        "comparison_df = te.run_training_and_report(\n",
        "    limit_per_class=2500,\n",
        "    seed=42,\n+        "    model_out_path='/content/models/best_sentiment_pipeline.joblib',\n",
        "    show_plots=True,\n+        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "comparison_df"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
